    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="0855" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-01T23:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1931—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—3:32 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. American Chargé in Bolivia in telegram dated July 1 states that Bolivia had
                    resolved to break off diplomatic relations with Paraguay, and to accept the
                    Argentine offer of arbitration.</p>
                <pb facs="0856" n="742" xml:id="pg742"/>
                <p>This evening the Under Secretary for Foreign Affairs informed me that Argentina
                    had not offered arbitration, and he added very confidentially that he doubted if
                    Argentina would consent to arbitrate if invited, because of Argentina’s
                    proximity to the disputed territory, and also because he thought that the
                    friendly American nations to whom the question had previously been submitted
                    should continue to function.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
